Figure 3 demonstrates that Nano-11 induces a transient inflammatory response at the injection site and is internalized by recruited immune cells. Panel A shows an early influx of neutrophils peaking at 6 hours, followed by a more prolonged accumulation of Mac-2+ macrophages, Ly6C+ monocytes, and antigen-presenting cells, all peaking around Day 2 before declining. Panel B, using confocal images, visually confirms that Nano-11 (red) is efficiently taken up by MHCII+ antigen-presenting cells, Ly6C+ monocytes, and Mac-2+ macrophages at various time points, supporting its role in immune cell targeting and activation following intramuscular injection.